/*****************************************************************************
    T1m -- MUTUAL RECURSION. The coverage question behind T1.

    field.recursive is INFERRED, not marked (aCTionTokenXP, ruleActions.rtn:882):
        if processingCode
            if ANYtoken.groupBody == currentMETHOD.groupBody
                currentMETHOD.recursive = true;
    That is identity against currentMETHOD -- DIRECT self-reference only. In
    A -> B -> A neither action names itself, so NEITHER gets flagged, so
    saveLocalFields never runs and re-entering walkA clobbers its live locals.

    Same tree and same expected trace as T1, only routed through two actions:
        A trunk / B leafA / A i / A j / B leafB / A k / A l      = 7
    walkA(trunk) is still live when walkA(i) runs, so this re-enters walkA
    exactly as T1 re-enters walk -- but without the flag.

    7 in that order -> the inference covers mutual recursion after all.
    Anything else   -> per-frame is real but its COVERAGE is direct-only, and
                       every mutually recursive walk silently loses locals.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(IterTest);
define
    leafA   i j;
    leafB   k l;
    trunk   leafA leafB;

    walkA argument code={
        print "A " taG argument:;
        iterate grup on argument;
        while ++grup
            walkB(grup);
        };

    walkB argument code={
        print "B " taG argument:;
        iterate grup on argument;
        while ++grup
            walkA(grup);
        };
    ;

walkA(trunk);
stop();
